{"type":"text","timestamp":1787412934170,"sessionID":"ses_fd5e4b0b7ffe2Y0MulRCIM2VNV","part":{"id":"prt_02a1cea01001DT3kE8gzbAPb8S","messageID":"msg_02a1cdea7001wGrHURKUZwsd92","sessionID":"ses_fd5e4b0b7ffe2Y0MulRCIM2VNV","type":"text","text":"All requirements are met and no new test failures were introduced (the 5 failures are pre-existing). Summary of changes in `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- Added `withoutExtras` to strip `onResult`/`onMatch`/`onIgnore`/`ignore` from options so the ignore matcher never inherits the caller's callbacks (no recursive evaluation).\n- Added `wrapExtras` to apply ignore logic and fire the lifecycle callbacks exactly once per input, building a result object carrying `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, `isMatch` (final decision) plus `isIgnored`.\n- `onIgnore` fires only when a pattern match is overridden by an ignore; a true non-match is reported as `isMatch:false`/`isIgnored:false`, never as ignored.\n- Array patterns and the `returnObject` form retain their original return types (boolean for arrays, result object for single patterns); only the new extras are layered on.","time":{"start":1787412933121,"end":1787412934165}}}
